WEBVTT

00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:07.310
What's wrong?

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.370
<i>The capital...</i>

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:32.760
<i>is burning...</i>

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:35.880
<i>It's all burning...</i>

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:50.270
Tsushima... is done for...

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.410
<i>Another force?</i>

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:57.010
<i>Ten warships, and over 
a thousand Mongol warriors.</i>

00:00:57.010 --> 00:00:58.910
<i>They never stood a chance.</i>

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:07.160
Shiraishi-dono, we need 
to head somewhere else...

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:13.970
I'm... sorry.

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:20.540
When I was a ruler, I had a city 
I'd built from scratch taken from me,

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:23.370
and my mansion and 
my people burned in the flames.

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:25.890
This reminds me of that...

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:34.920
Princess Teruhi!

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.470
You're back!

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:38.720
Genpachi.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:40.800
You're safe...

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:41.660
Yes...

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:43.990
The capital's survivors 
are over there, as well.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:28.730
Abiru Yajirou-dono!

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:30.430
I'm glad you're all right.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:35.340
I came back alive, and now 
I've nowhere to go home.

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:37.720
Is this all the survivors from the capital?

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:39.420
Yeah, that's right.

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:41.170
I don't know what happened to the others.

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:44.920
I'm sure some of them 
made it into the mountains...

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:46.560
What happened?

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:50.160
This morning, Mongol ships 
attacked the capital.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:54.450
We returned from Sasu 
after an all-night march.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:55.930
And as soon as we did...

00:03:56.770 --> 00:04:02.420
The Mongols intended to attack both 
Sasu and the capital from the start.

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:08.130
That's a lot of effort 
for a tiny, little island.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:10.490
What a pain in the ass!

00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:13.710
How long are these damn 
Mongols going to stay here?

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:15.560
For days and weeks.

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:19.260
They'll be here for days and weeks,

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:22.670
and they'll spend every hour 
they're here slaughtering us.

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:28.740
They want to kill everyone 
on the island! I know it!

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:36.450
So it didn't matter what we did, huh?

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:39.940
No matter how much 
we struggle, everyone dies!

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:43.960
The whole battle at Sasu 
was just a waste of time!

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:47.380
It was a waste of time to even fight back!

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:51.250
You little brat...

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:54.240
What are you willing to fight for, then?

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.810
Just to keep yourself alive a little longer?

00:04:57.410 --> 00:05:00.180
A life like that is what's 
really a waste of time.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:02.740
What?

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:05.340
Shut your mouth, exile.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:07.030
Don't even try.

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:10.410
It's a waste of time to fight 
somebody stronger than you, right?

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:12.820
Damn you!

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:13.740
Abiru-dono!

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:15.230
Reporting!

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:16.500
The Mongols are coming!

00:05:22.190 --> 00:05:23.190
Get down!

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:28.750
<i>Five of them... Scouts.</i>

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:31.810
<i>They're dressed differently 
than the ones we saw at Sasu.</i>

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:42.020
They're turning back!

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:43.490
Good.

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:44.830
Princess...

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:50.400
They took them from me...

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:53.540
My father, my brother...

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:56.080
My people, my land...

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:59.060
And my heart...

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:01.760
Everything!

00:06:02.510 --> 00:06:04.180
Everything!

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:04.960
Princess!

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:06.960
Damn you!

00:06:07.810 --> 00:06:09.110
I won't let you go!

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:12.840
Princess!

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:14.350
More!

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:15.920
More!

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:19.280
Don't let the scouts escape!

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:21.550
One fled!

00:06:21.550 --> 00:06:23.090
Can you do it, Hitari?

00:06:23.090 --> 00:06:24.320
I'm willing to try.

00:06:32.170 --> 00:06:34.760
They were able to turn the horses 
around on a narrow mountain path,

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:36.860
and fire arrows behind them 
while galloping away.

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:39.160
They're skilled horsemen.

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:44.150
It smells like milk!

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:47.100
They don't weave their hair 
like Goryeo people, either.

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:49.200
They probably don't speak 
the same language, either.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:51.500
And they probably don't fight the same way.

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:53.540
One of the horses fled.

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:54.380
Yeah.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:56.880
If a horse comes back with no rider, 
they'll know something's up.

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:58.560
You mustn't, Princess!

00:06:58.970 --> 00:07:00.660
Your wound will open again.

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:04.240
I couldn't control myself...

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:08.480
I'm sorry, everyone!

00:07:12.590 --> 00:07:14.830
It won't change anything.

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:17.500
They noticed us.

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:20.750
That's why they turned 
around all of a sudden.

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:22.730
Princess, we must tend to your wounds...

00:07:22.010 --> 00:07:30.270
<i>More importantly, what that girl just did 
changed the looks on everybody's faces.</i>

00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:31.400
But where do we go?

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:33.590
Why not Aso Bay to the north?

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:36.390
There are provisions 
and places to hide there.

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:37.730
A good idea.

00:07:37.730 --> 00:07:40.620
When that's done, we can disguise 
the shortcuts to the north,

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:42.510
and then stop the Mongols here.

00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:44.010
Not happening.

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:46.090
Who are you?

00:07:46.090 --> 00:07:47.420
Who am I?

00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:48.640
I'm more important than you country samurai.

00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:51.670
Amushi, can you see the Mongols 
movements from up there?

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:52.310
Yep.

00:07:52.750 --> 00:07:54.830
Run? Hide the shortcuts?

00:07:54.830 --> 00:07:56.920
You don't have time.

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:06.590
<b>Mongol Mingghan Commander
Uriyan Edei</b>

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:07.890
Hurry!

00:08:07.890 --> 00:08:09.900
We're heading for Aso Bay!

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:18.490
What's wrong, old lady?

00:08:18.490 --> 00:08:20.820
I'll stay here.

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:23.910
I lost my child and my grandchild.

00:08:23.910 --> 00:08:28.980
I'd rather choose a place to die 
myself than let the Mongols kill me.

00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:30.760
<i>How noble...</i>

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:32.590
Yajirou-dono.

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:35.790
We can stay here to hold them off.

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:39.710
On this narrow mountain road, their 
superior numbers will do them no good.

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:42.260
Yeah, you're right.

00:08:42.260 --> 00:08:46.050
If we don't delay them, 
they'll catch up to the fleeing people.

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:48.200
You exiles must work, too.

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:50.450
You serious?

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:55.920
You intend to have us work 
for free again, don't you?

00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:58.680
I ain't doing this forever.

00:09:06.170 --> 00:09:07.030
Let me go!

00:09:07.030 --> 00:09:09.430
I knew you'd do that, old man.

00:09:09.430 --> 00:09:12.020
When they were burning down 
the capital, you were robbing it!

00:09:14.890 --> 00:09:19.200
I'll take that treasure off your hands.

00:09:21.980 --> 00:09:25.240
Well done, considering we 
didn't have much time.

00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:26.610
It's light, too.

00:09:26.610 --> 00:09:29.740
We made them like you said to, sir...

00:09:29.740 --> 00:09:31.560
But what are these?

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:34.970
A makeshift long weapon 
used in the Gikei style.

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:35.870
It's called a spear.

00:09:35.870 --> 00:09:36.630
A spear?

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:40.180
Abiru Yajirou, you wanted 
to stop the enemy here, right?

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:42.330
Yes.

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:44.240
If you want to protect yourself,

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:46.840
you need to be prepared 
to sacrifice yourself.

00:09:47.690 --> 00:09:50.970
We'll build a fort on this path to seal it.

00:09:53.970 --> 00:09:55.800
Build a fort?

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:57.850
The enemy's right here.

00:09:57.850 --> 00:10:00.330
It's 80 percent done.

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:02.200
Right here.

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:21.060
Everybody's in position, right?

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:22.710
Once I pull the enemy in,

00:10:22.710 --> 00:10:23.770
follow the plan!

00:10:23.770 --> 00:10:25.600
Everyone, stay sharp!

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:31.400
Hey, new kid.

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:33.210
You ain't looking good.

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:34.740
Get to the rear.

00:10:34.740 --> 00:10:36.520
Shut up!

00:10:36.520 --> 00:10:38.230
I can't let you do this alone!

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:40.650
Here they come!

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:46.240
They're up ahead.

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:48.040
Everyone...

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:51.330
Protect this single corner the best you can.

00:10:51.730 --> 00:10:54.200
Tell yourself that if we're lucky, 
we can defeat the Mongol's huge army

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:55.850
and take back the capital.

00:10:56.190 --> 00:10:58.080
If you can't convince yourself of that,

00:10:58.080 --> 00:11:00.000
you won't even be able 
to protect this single corner.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.670
Are you ready, Abiru Yajirou?

00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:10.850
<i>They're all fat and strong.</i>

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:13.350
<i>They're just ordinary soldiers, 
but they attack with no hesitation.</i>

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:15.230
<i>They're skilled warriors.</i>

00:11:15.230 --> 00:11:15.900
They're coming!

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:16.790
Right!

00:11:25.840 --> 00:11:27.670
I see.

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:30.910
When the Mongols round the corner,

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:32.820
they use their swordsmen to pin them down,

00:11:32.820 --> 00:11:35.300
and then strike from the side with arrows?

00:11:35.300 --> 00:11:39.200
Kuchii-dono says it's called 
the Yokoyagake, the side arrow attack.

00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:42.720
Arrows from the side, huh? 
Sounds about right.

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:45.490
Okay, I've seen what there is to see.

00:11:45.490 --> 00:11:47.590
Time for me to get going.

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:51.050
Stab upwards!

00:11:56.230 --> 00:11:58.690
This is a lot of fun to use.

00:12:06.650 --> 00:12:08.740
There's more! Stay sharp!

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:14.750
Every minute we do this gives 
the people more time to escape.

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:18.670
But...

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:20.480
It's just a dead end!

00:12:24.140 --> 00:12:27.840
What waits at the end of this battle?

00:12:28.130 --> 00:12:29.440
Hey, General.

00:12:29.950 --> 00:12:32.760
Don't fight a war unless 
you know why you're fighting it.

00:12:32.760 --> 00:12:34.800
If you feel any hesitation at all,

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:37.370
run away and follow the rest of the people,

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:40.530
or run off on your own. 
Whatever you want to do.

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:55.420
Kuchii Jinzaburou!

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:56.210
What?

00:12:56.630 --> 00:13:01.820
What makes you able to risk 
your life for a battle with no future?

00:13:02.850 --> 00:13:06.330
You're not from this island! 
Why are you willing to—

00:13:11.810 --> 00:13:16.440
9th Year of Bun'ei, February, Kamakura

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:21.630
You beat me.

00:13:22.710 --> 00:13:26.230
Kuchii Jinzaburou may be a famous warrior,

00:13:26.230 --> 00:13:28.920
but he's terrible at shogi, huh?

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:33.280
Shogi and war are two 
completely different things.

00:13:33.280 --> 00:13:38.570
Your father said they were the same.

00:13:39.650 --> 00:13:40.710
My father did?

00:13:40.710 --> 00:13:41.840
Yes.

00:13:41.340 --> 00:13:53.060
<b>Houjou Clan Branch Family
Nagoe Tokiaki</b>

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:45.620
To be honest, he was a lot better than you,

00:13:45.620 --> 00:13:49.360
but you play shogi in a very similar way.

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:52.400
The bonds of blood are strange things.

00:13:53.630 --> 00:13:55.410
Is that so?

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:58.140
To be honest, I barely remember his face.

00:13:59.010 --> 00:14:04.080
I see a lot of Tasaburou in you.

00:14:04.630 --> 00:14:07.690
Oh, you've truly lost this one.

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:09.650
Kimitoki-dono!

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:16.580
<b>Tokiaki's Son 
Nagoe Kimitoki</b>

00:14:09.650 --> 00:14:12.950
Jinzaburou, if you can't get to the point 
where he'll deliberately let you win,

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:15.340
you're going to have 
trouble getting promoted.

00:14:16.570 --> 00:14:18.140
Kimitoki.

00:14:18.140 --> 00:14:20.590
Don't tell him that.

00:14:20.590 --> 00:14:22.590
I'm sorry, Father.

00:14:26.580 --> 00:14:28.600
I'll see you soon, then.

00:14:28.600 --> 00:14:29.600
Jinzaburou.

00:14:30.770 --> 00:14:33.000
Stay away from our family for a while.

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:36.040
You're not the social type,

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:39.450
but you've been visiting often lately.

00:14:39.450 --> 00:14:44.060
It's because the shogun's aide, 
Tokimune, has it out for us, right?

00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:50.300
Thirty years ago, 
we rebelled against his clan.

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:55.020
The rift between clans is something 
that is passed down through the years.

00:14:55.020 --> 00:15:01.050
That's why I'd like you to avoid doing 
anything that could provoke a reaction.

00:15:01.050 --> 00:15:02.500
But Tokiaki-dono...

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:05.080
Look around our mansion.

00:15:05.890 --> 00:15:08.300
We don't even use the 
archery grounds anymore.

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:11.080
I planted flowers,

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:14.000
and soon they will cover the whole area.

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:18.220
You understand, right, Jinzaburou?

00:15:18.740 --> 00:15:23.800
We don't want to give him 
the slightest excuse for war.

00:15:26.490 --> 00:15:27.500
As you wish.

00:15:28.600 --> 00:15:30.480
But, Tokiaki-dono...

00:15:31.140 --> 00:15:33.380
They say that if you truly 
wish to not draw your sword,

00:15:33.380 --> 00:15:35.020
you must keep it at your side.

00:15:35.510 --> 00:15:38.440
Please make sure you 
do not abandon your sword.

00:15:40.220 --> 00:15:42.080
Farewell.

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:59.720
Kuchii Jinzaburou-dono.

00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:03.150
Oh, if it isn't Ookura Yorisue.

00:16:03.530 --> 00:16:05.180
A servant of the Houjou Clan...

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:06.980
<b>Servant of the Houjou Clan  
Ookura Yorisue</b>

00:16:05.180 --> 00:16:06.970
Not someone I'd preferred to have run into.

00:16:06.970 --> 00:16:10.510
Yeah. They're in the service 
of the shogun's aide,

00:16:10.510 --> 00:16:12.150
and they'll never let you forget it.

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:19.760
I've heard you've been playing a lot 
of shogi with Nagoe Tokiaki-dono.

00:16:19.760 --> 00:16:23.040
I'm sure he's not a very fun opponent.

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:25.630
I would be happy to play you sometime.

00:16:25.630 --> 00:16:29.340
No, I'm a terrible player.

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:30.900
I'd be embarrassed.

00:16:30.900 --> 00:16:33.750
Come by any time, and I'll teach you.

00:16:34.390 --> 00:16:37.760
Both in war and in shogi, 
the larger picture is what's important.

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:40.690
No matter how good of a fighter 
you are on your own,

00:16:40.690 --> 00:16:42.970
you're still just a pawn.

00:16:48.550 --> 00:16:51.210
<i>It's clear he's planning something.</i>

00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:54.080
<i>But when will he act?</i>

00:16:55.200 --> 00:17:01.660
Several Days Later:
February 11th Around 10:00 In the Morning

00:17:07.870 --> 00:17:09.870
Nagoe Tokiaki-dono!

00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:13.640
How dare you plot rebellion 
against Tokimune-sama?!

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:14.820
Impossible!

00:17:14.820 --> 00:17:16.790
When did we rebel against him?

00:17:16.790 --> 00:17:19.430
Where in this mansion 
can you see evidence of that?

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:21.860
Ookura Yorisue!

00:17:21.860 --> 00:17:23.410
Let me see Tokimune!

00:17:23.410 --> 00:17:25.430
He can clear up this misunderstanding!

00:17:27.130 --> 00:17:28.310
Father...

00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:35.770
We can find what exactly it is you're 
plotting after we have your head.

00:17:36.920 --> 00:17:37.820
Do it!

00:17:44.110 --> 00:17:46.740
Oh, Ookura-dono.

00:17:46.740 --> 00:17:50.530
I came by to learn some shogi.

00:17:50.960 --> 00:17:52.540
Jinzaburou!

00:17:53.250 --> 00:17:56.360
Men, we are the army of the shogun's aide!

00:17:56.360 --> 00:17:59.880
Capture that criminal 
and win glory for yourself!

00:18:08.780 --> 00:18:10.780
Ookura Yorisue!

00:18:12.310 --> 00:18:14.530
Stop it, Jinzaburou!

00:18:16.560 --> 00:18:18.450
Kimitoki-dono!

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:23.950
The more of them you kill, 
the worse our position becomes.

00:18:24.280 --> 00:18:26.860
So you knelt there in fear

00:18:27.380 --> 00:18:29.850
when your father was about to be killed?

00:18:29.850 --> 00:18:31.300
You were there the whole time?

00:18:31.300 --> 00:18:34.470
I must protect the clan!

00:18:38.490 --> 00:18:41.020
Your death will be a slow one.

00:18:41.020 --> 00:18:44.350
In the name of the shogun's aide,
 you will be punished!

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:49.850
Now take Tokiaki's head!

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:50.650
Yes, sir!

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:56.720
Jinzaburou, I told you that 
you played shogi like your father,

00:18:56.720 --> 00:18:58.850
but some things about you are different.

00:18:58.850 --> 00:19:02.360
You're never willing to sacrifice 
a piece when you play.

00:19:02.760 --> 00:19:05.330
That's why you're so bad.

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:08.380
But I found that fascinating.

00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:12.550
If you say you don't remember 
your father's face,

00:19:12.550 --> 00:19:15.400
then think of my face instead,

00:19:15.400 --> 00:19:17.750
and remember me in your 
heart as your father.

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:36.480
If you throw down your sword 
when there's a sword at your throat,

00:19:36.480 --> 00:19:38.020
everything will be taken from you.

00:19:39.130 --> 00:19:41.430
Even a child knows this.

00:19:41.430 --> 00:19:43.690
And once, I was forced 
to learn it for myself.

00:19:43.690 --> 00:19:45.120
That's why I fight.

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:46.870
There's nothing more to it than that.

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:50.900
That is the way I fight. The answer I found.

00:19:52.220 --> 00:19:53.740
Abiru Yajirou.

00:19:53.740 --> 00:19:57.250
If you're a general, no, a samurai...

00:19:57.250 --> 00:19:59.580
Your war is your own.

00:19:59.580 --> 00:20:01.310
Decide for yourself what it will be!

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:05.150
They're here!

00:20:08.270 --> 00:20:09.140
Torches?

00:20:09.510 --> 00:20:11.850
They're different than the ones before.

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:17.660
Oh, no! Those are...

00:20:18.790 --> 00:20:20.780
Keep them away from us!

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:31.200
Get behind your shields!

00:20:35.680 --> 00:20:38.410
The path is open! Charge!

00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:45.880
I can't see anything!

00:20:45.880 --> 00:20:47.290
Is anyone here?

00:20:53.910 --> 00:20:57.130
If they have an open path to go through, 
they'll crush us with their numbers!

00:20:58.220 --> 00:21:00.020
Everybody who's still breathing, stand!

00:21:00.020 --> 00:21:03.270
I'll block the path they opened!

00:21:04.790 --> 00:21:05.660
Yajirou?

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:07.950
Don't worry, men.

00:21:07.950 --> 00:21:12.410
We faced these "explosives" at Sasu.

00:21:12.410 --> 00:21:14.410
We learned a little about how to avoid them.

00:21:15.300 --> 00:21:17.740
All it does is make a loud noise.

00:21:17.740 --> 00:21:19.020
If you don't let it hit you,

00:21:19.020 --> 00:21:20.450
it doesn't hurt at all.

00:21:20.450 --> 00:21:21.170
Right!

00:21:24.270 --> 00:21:26.100
They're trapped, with nowhere to run.

00:21:30.090 --> 00:21:31.850
Now kill them all!

00:21:41.840 --> 00:21:48.770
I just realized now how powerful 
my clan's warriors are!

00:21:48.770 --> 00:21:52.450
I wasn't worthy to lead them.

00:21:52.940 --> 00:21:56.980
A general doesn't worry about the meaning 
of a battle in the middle of the fight...

00:21:57.400 --> 00:21:58.860
That's the job of a poet!

00:21:59.730 --> 00:22:01.790
Look forward, Jinzaburou!

00:22:04.590 --> 00:22:06.670
Let me protect your back!

00:22:07.010 --> 00:22:10.010
<b>Episode 5:
Resolve</b>
